.TH TASK-LAUNCHER 1 "October 2026" "task-launcher 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
task-launcher \- R.A.I.N./T.A.S.K. application launcher (rain-core client)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B task-launcher
[\fB\-\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-maximized\fR | \fB\-\-windowed\fR | \fB\-\-fullscreen\fR] [\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Native Qt launcher showing the R.A.I.N. app tiles, the rain-core link state and the network
state. It is an ordinary desktop window: it does not replace the compositor, the session or
the login manager, and it never runs as root. The launcher itself never opens hardware and
never transmits: device state comes from rain-core, and the field apps it starts (rain-mesh,
FoxtrotGPS, SDR++, Gqrx) open their devices themselves.
.PP
Native windows: Library (discovers a local kiwix-serve; loopback only), Radio / APRS
(Direwolf status and a receive-only KISS monitor), Weather (local tools and data age; no
forecast) and Medical (offline reference finder; no patient data).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-socket " " \fIPATH\fR
rain-core socket (default /run/rain/core.sock).
.TP
.B \-\-maximized
Start maximized (default unless changed in Settings).
.TP
.B \-\-windowed
Start in a normal window.
.TP
.B \-\-fullscreen
Start fullscreen. F11 toggles, Esc leaves fullscreen.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/task-launcher/apps.d/*.toml
Shipped app manifests.
.TP
.I /etc/task-launcher/apps.d/*.toml
Administrator manifests (replace shipped ones with the same id).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/task-launcher/apps.d/*.toml
Per-user manifests (new ids only).
.TP
.I /etc/task-launcher/branding.toml
System default branding (see /usr/share/doc/task-launcher/examples/branding.toml).
.TP
.I ~/.config/task-launcher/settings.json, tiles.json
Per-user settings and tile layout.
.TP
.I ~/.config/task-launcher/reference.toml
Optional folders for the Medical and Weather windows ([medical] dirs, [weather] dirs). Read only.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/task-launcher/
Launcher log and per-app logs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rain-console (1)
